Part 1 — Creating JSON
The journal creates a JavaScript object containing:
name = Romal
age = 20
dept = IT

and then uses JSON.stringify() in three different ways.     BDNS Journal
Step 2 — Create creating.html
<html>

<head>

    <title>Creating JSON</title>

</head>

<body>

<script type="text/javascript">

    var data = {
        "name": "Romal",
        "age": 20,
        "dept": "IT"
    };

    document.writeln(JSON.stringify(data) + "<br>");

    document.writeln(
        JSON.stringify(data, ["name", "age", "dept"]) + "<br>"
    );

    document.writeln(
        JSON.stringify(data, ["name", "age", "dept"], 5)
    );

</script>

</body>

</html>

This follows the journal's Creating JSON program.     BDNS Journal
